  body: "# Application period for DMG revision\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured revision guidance uses
    the date of notification, requests for written reasons and accepted late applications to describe how an application
    period is established.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis is a temporal dependency record, not a deadline calculator.
    Notification evidence, benefit-specific provisions, late-application conditions, any-time revision and effective
    dates must be considered separately.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 03060, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n- [DMG 03061, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n- [DMG 03063, PDF page 14](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=14)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of the 15 September
    2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance, not a consolidated
    statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an
    entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file positions. Machine
    extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve extracted text;
    no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability remain
    separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch3` PDF SHA-256: `4aebcf1988fb7d96698dce77bf88d68272a5975171decc42f58c32cfa1d42eeb`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `444fa1a240db31b94cb75c13a2f2ece7c691f15aeca0bec2dd298e2f4e08f66a`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source states that timing determines how an application for revision is dealt with, rather
      than imposing one undifferentiated cut-off.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0014
      quote: "03060 Claimants can apply for revision of decisions if they think they are wrong or unfair. The timing
        of\nthe application determines how it is dealt with by the DM. For appeals to FtT, UT and the Courts see
        DMG\nChapter 06."
      locator: DMG 03060
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0014
      quote: "03061 Where an application is made outside the time limits in DMG 03063 et seq , the DM should\nconsider
        the ‘any time’ revision procedure. Where this is not applicable the DM should consider whether\nthe decision
        can be superseded."
      locator: DMG 03061
